When `valid == 0`, all threads initialize their slots to zero and synchronize. Thread zero executes an empty summation loop and writes `output[0] = 0.0f`; the host neither initializes the output nor skips the kernel. At `valid == 96`, all 96 input entries are loaded and summed in increasing index order using floating-point addition.

